60
00:04:29,180 --> 00:04:30,040
Like, it was hard.

61
00:04:30,840 --> 00:04:40,420
And when we really got a hold of our lives in Christ and surrendered our lives, we had this wild thought that we need to calculate our back tithe.

62
00:04:40,420 --> 00:04:45,620
So I was 29 when I surrendered my life to Jesus.

63
00:04:45,620 --> 00:04:49,780
And I've pretty much worked full time since I was 18.

64
00:04:49,780 --> 00:04:54,380
There's been pockets of maybe a month or so where I might not have had a job.

65
00:04:54,380 --> 00:04:58,660
But pretty much since I was actually 15, I'm sorry, till 29 I worked.

66
00:04:58,660 --> 00:04:59,820
Full time 18.

67
00:05:00,220 --> 00:05:01,380
And the same with my wife.

68
00:05:01,380 --> 00:05:02,880
Pretty much since high school working.

69
00:05:02,880 --> 00:05:05,680
So we calculated out back tithe.

70
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:13,840
And we came up with it was less, about almost $400 a month for like 10 years we felt like we owed God.

71
00:05:13,840 --> 00:05:17,960
And I mean, I'm laughing about this now, but we were dead serious.

72
00:05:17,960 --> 00:05:20,860
We're like, we're going to pay back tithe.

73
00:05:20,860 --> 00:05:26,720
Because we are so convicted of not giving in to who God is.

74
00:05:27,500 --> 00:05:33,940
At times in our life, we would mail money to her grandmother because she was like our spiritual sort of connection at the time.

75
00:05:33,940 --> 00:05:39,000
We tithe $20 to her family here and there because we just felt like we were giving to God.

76
00:05:39,160 --> 00:05:41,700
So we came up with our number.

77
00:05:41,700 --> 00:05:43,000
We wrote a check.

78
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:44,460
We gave it to the church.

79
00:05:44,460 --> 00:05:46,360
And that check bounced.

80
00:05:46,360 --> 00:05:51,000
You want to talk about embarrassment.

81
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:55,080
That like we were still sort of new to the church.

82
00:05:55,080 --> 00:05:56,940
We'd only been there like less than a year.

83
00:05:57,160 --> 00:06:00,740
And we had given before and those checks went through.

84
00:06:00,740 --> 00:06:03,200
But this check bounced.

85
00:06:03,200 --> 00:06:06,540
And that really made us reflect back.

86
00:06:06,540 --> 00:06:10,860
Were we doing it out of our own will and desire, which is fine.

87
00:06:10,860 --> 00:06:18,460
Or were we like out of compulsion and need versus out of the generosity of what God's actually done.

88
00:06:18,900 --> 00:06:28,320
And so we didn't need a lot of discernment to see God saying, I don't need you to pay me back tithe.

89
00:06:28,320 --> 00:06:30,780
You don't owe me money.

90
00:06:30,780 --> 00:06:36,420
And if there was interest on that, it might have been a little higher payment for maybe 30 years.

91
00:06:38,300 --> 00:06:41,180
But, you know, God is generous.

92
00:06:41,180 --> 00:06:46,220
And he doesn't require things like he did under the law.

93
00:06:46,220 --> 00:06:48,840
Like he did before.

94
00:06:48,840 --> 00:06:54,880
There's a beautiful story in 1 Kings, or 2 Kings 22 with Josiah.

95
00:06:54,880 --> 00:06:59,260
And many people see Josiah as this king that brought reformation, and he did.

96
00:06:59,260 --> 00:07:00,760
But he saw this.

97
00:07:03,260 --> 00:07:10,140
When they were redoing the temple, they tore down a wall, and they found the book of the law in the wall.

98
00:07:10,140 --> 00:07:12,980
Which is wild that the Bible was hidden in a wall.

99
00:07:12,980 --> 00:07:18,500
And then when he read it, Josiah tore his clothes, or in fact had it read to him.

100
00:07:18,500 --> 00:07:25,080
He tore his clothes, and he laid on the floor, and he was, you know, just absolutely grieved at what he was hearing.

101
00:07:25,080 --> 00:07:27,080
But it was called the book of the law.

102
00:07:27,080 --> 00:07:31,820
And then later in that chapter, the beginning or the next, I can't remember if it's the end or the beginning.

103
00:07:32,280 --> 00:07:35,380
The language changes from book of the law to book of the covenant.

104
00:07:35,380 --> 00:07:38,960
And that's the perspective that we have with God.

105
00:07:38,960 --> 00:07:44,000
That it's not law under compulsion, but it's covenant, which is love.

106
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:48,500
And so as you've been journeying, this is the third week of generosity.

107
00:07:48,500 --> 00:07:56,500
We see God as a covenantal God, not as this law God that comes down to smite us because we've done wrong.

108
00:07:56,500 --> 00:07:57,680
Amen?

109
00:07:58,680 --> 00:08:04,400
So like I said, this is the third week that you're in this process of practicing the way.

