173
00:13:53,120 --> 00:13:54,760
He says,

174
00:13:54,760 --> 00:13:58,960
Truly, I tell you, he will dress himself to serve.

175
00:13:58,960 --> 00:14:00,240
Sorry.

176
00:14:00,240 --> 00:14:04,380
Truly, I tell you, he will dress himself to serve,

177
00:14:04,380 --> 00:14:09,220
will have them recline at the table, and will come wait on them.

178
00:14:09,220 --> 00:14:09,960
Wait a minute.

179
00:14:11,020 --> 00:14:13,080
So when the master comes back,

180
00:14:13,080 --> 00:14:17,400
it's not the servants that are waiting on the master,

181
00:14:17,400 --> 00:14:19,280
waiting for them to come home.

182
00:14:19,280 --> 00:14:23,260
No, when the master returns, sees that his servants were doing their thing,

183
00:14:23,260 --> 00:14:24,320
and he was like, no, no, no.

184
00:14:24,320 --> 00:14:28,980
You sit, you recline, and I'm going to wait on you.

185
00:14:28,980 --> 00:14:32,820
That's a paradigm shift for them.

186
00:14:32,820 --> 00:14:35,520
Think about first century people.

187
00:14:35,520 --> 00:14:36,640
This is us.

188
00:14:36,640 --> 00:14:42,940
We can really begin to think about whether it's some rich aristocrat that has something,

189
00:14:42,940 --> 00:14:43,720
and then they're serving them.

190
00:14:43,720 --> 00:14:45,400
But think about this from their perspective,

191
00:14:45,400 --> 00:14:48,780
because they don't have some of the same language and things that we have today.

192
00:14:49,800 --> 00:14:55,080
Jesus is telling them that, wait a minute, the master is going to be the one doing the serving.

193
00:14:55,080 --> 00:14:57,580
That shifts their minds.

194
00:15:00,120 --> 00:15:07,200
I'm not a gambling man, but I'm going to bet you that they were very confused when Jesus said these words.

195
00:15:07,200 --> 00:15:12,300
Truly, I tell you, he will dress to himself to serve.

196
00:15:12,300 --> 00:15:15,140
That means that he's not just walking to the door to serve.

197
00:15:15,220 --> 00:15:18,160
That means that he's going to get changed out of his wedding garments,

198
00:15:18,160 --> 00:15:21,420
because there were specific clothes that you wore to weddings,

199
00:15:21,420 --> 00:15:24,900
to get into servants' garments, and then I'm going to serve.

200
00:15:24,900 --> 00:15:29,100
You would think later on that when Jesus washed their feet,

201
00:15:29,100 --> 00:15:31,040
they might have been a little bit more prepared for that.

202
00:15:31,040 --> 00:15:36,060
But this, this even, let's keep going.

203
00:15:36,600 --> 00:15:41,020
This is truly an upside down, the master role of Jesus,

204
00:15:41,020 --> 00:15:44,140
totally flipping the script on what's going on

205
00:15:44,140 --> 00:15:46,660
